# Part 5 — Can more be presented?

## 5.1 The constraint, stated first

Three limits govern every candidate, and they point in different directions.

**Upstream cost is per request, not per channel.** Fifteen HTTP calls per snapshot
is a compile-time constant (`snapshot.ts:12-16`). Folding an operand into an
existing bundle in `queries.ts` costs **zero extra calls**; only a new `labelled`
query costs one. The real ceiling is evaluation time: the per-query budget
defaults to 5 s (`config.ts:44`) and the worst scrape on this cluster already
takes 1.46 s, so a bundle cannot grow indefinitely. Assumption, not measured: a
bundle of ~12 operands is still comfortable. The measurement that would settle it
is the `duration` on `/api/v1/query` for the extended expression.

**Anything reaching a material key must have a finite, enumerable codomain.**
This is the invariant `live/bind.ts:1-33` exists to hold, and it is why colour is
driven by `status` and opacity by a single constant. Five materials are requested
per module per build (`materials.ts:218`); binding a continuous number to colour
or opacity allocates a fresh set every tick — 140 per tick at 28 modules.
`MaterialRegistry.sweep()` is the backstop, not the fix. So **new appearance
bindings are the expensive kind of change**, and the cheap surfaces are elsewhere.

**Geometry is not free either.** Radius, arc and band height reach
`cylinderGeometry args` (`Strip.tsx:177`). Args are compared element-wise, so
equal values cost nothing — but a *changed* value reconstructs the geometry
instance. A continuously-varying geometry binding is per-tick geometry churn, and
that is why the scene's silhouette stays authored.

What that leaves as genuinely free:

| Surface | Status | Capacity |
|---|---|---|
| **The panel** | exists, renders no channel data | unlimited, zero GPU cost |
| The `<Contact>` lane | built and tested, commented out at `Strip.tsx:267-281` | a second visual plane, already keyed by lane |
| `glow` / `halo` / `trail` booleans | authored, per-module | finite codomain, so material-safe |
| Rotation | taken by `rate` | narrow band, low legibility (Part 1.2) |
| Colour / opacity | taken, codomain-bounded | closed by construction |
| Band label text | `LabelFactory` caches per string | **unbounded codomain — do not bind** |

One more guard rail: `queries.spec.ts` fails the build on a bundle signal with no
consumer (`queries.ts:192-196` explains why). Operand and channel land together,
which is the right coupling and should be preserved.

